Implemented US-108 as the selected non-UI item 7 slice.

Changed:
- Added Supabase-backed cron auto-class discovery at `app/infrastructure/inngest/month-advance.ts:405`.
- Added runtime discovery wiring at `app/infrastructure/inngest/month-advance.ts:424`.
- Added `executeMonthAdvanceAutoClassDiscoveryHandoff` at `app/infrastructure/inngest/month-advance.ts:439`, dispatching ready auto classes through the existing Inngest auto handoff and sanitizing provider failures.
- Updated `/api/cron/month-advance` to use discovery when no explicit class/month params are supplied while preserving targeted explicit proof at `app/api/cron/month-advance/route.ts:29` and `app/api/cron/month-advance/route.ts:99`.
- Added focused tests in `app/infrastructure/inngest/month-advance.test.ts`.
- Added `docs/stories/US-108-cron-auto-class-discovery.md`.
- Updated `docs/TEST_MATRIX.md`, `docs/stories/backlog.md`, product docs, and the round-180 sprint log.

Validation:
- `npm run test:unit -- app/infrastructure/inngest/month-advance.test.ts` passed: 1 file, 20 tests.
- `npm run validate:quick` passed: 52 files, 530 tests.

One issue was found and fixed during validation: TypeScript hit an excessively deep Supabase client type instantiation, so I tightened the discovery reader’s boundary with a narrow local client type cast. No commit, push, or PR was created.

